# Keep the graphify knowledge graph scoped to the app + real docs, so every rebuild
# (/graphify . or --update) stays consistent instead of re-ingesting scaffolding.
# See CLAUDE.md "Knowledge graph".

# Process / tooling scaffolding — not repo architecture
.superpowers/
.claude/
.impeccable/

# Don't let graphify ingest its own output
graphify-out/

# devcycle working state (ledger, reports, findings, evidence) — local only, never committed
.devcycle/

# Planning artifacts — specs, plans and brainstorm notes stay local and untracked
docs/superpowers/

# Local maintenance audits — untracked snapshots of past drift; once fixed they would feed the graph stale claims
docs/audits/

# Per-session devcycle on-device verification output — local scratch, never committed
docs/*/on-device-checklist.md
docs/*/on-device-results.md

# The bundled spot snapshots are data exported from the database, not architecture; the scope's image entry is public/icon*.png
spotmap-website/public/spots/

# Local spot photos and their thumbnails. Git ignores them through spotmap-website/.gitignore,
# which graphify never reads: it reads .gitignore files only from the repo root down to the scan root.
# spots/*/* and not spots/*/: graphify matches with fnmatch, where * crosses /, so spots/*/ would
# also drop the committed spots/*.geojson, *.report.json and sources.json.
spotmap-website/data/thumbs/
spotmap-website/data/spots/*/*
